  "title": "Israel’s Election Deadlock: Gadi Eisenkot Tapped to Form Government",
  "summary": "Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has been chosen to form a government, despite the country's parliamentary election deadlock where neither party secured a majority. The election resulted in a stalemate, with neither man having a clear path to power.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Gadi Eisenkot is the strong opposition leader of Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition.",
